Chapter: ProbeIndirectUnder

 Is the defect confined to the over-apply path, or does the local-rooted
 path carry it too? emit-apply routes a FunTy result to emit-indirect-call
 when the callee is a LOCAL (Emit/X86_64Compound.codex:166-169), so a
 local closure entered with fewer arguments than it still wants goes
 through a different function than the top-level case.

 The control is the tree's own fixture shape
 (codex/plugs/test-input/partial.codex:9-10): bind the closure, then apply
 BOTH remaining arguments at once. It is green in-tree.

 The test splits that into two steps, so the closure is entered with one
 argument while it still wants two.

 `both 42` then `split 42` means the local path is sound and only the
 over-apply path is affected. `both 42` then anything else means the
 defect is in the closure representation rather than in one caller, and
 fixing a single application site cannot close it.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let h = add3 10
    in print-line-uni ("both 42 expected: " & show ((h 20) 12))
    let j = add3 10
    in let g = j 20
    in print-line-uni ("split 42 expected: " & show (g 12))
  end
